(review-verdict . approve)
(review-confidence . medium)
(findings . ((attempt-1-honesty . "the evidence record names the real failure mode of the previous run — surfaces written to the working tree but never committed to the delivery branch, evidence trio never created — and attempt-2 records the committed remediation (8231db41 topology report + prepared-env binding, 61be1eef release-surface sync); no attempt to relabel the failure as infra-only")
             (checksum-binding-verified . "every digest cited in the topology report was re-verified standalone this wave: w0 graph-snapshot, w1/w2/w3 dag-checkpoints, w4 shard-measurement (5/5 OK) and the integrated C2 binding (4/4 OK with sha256sum -c); the report's byte-for-byte claim is true, not aspirational")
             (evidence-coverage-wording . "the report claims record coverage for w0/w1/w2/w4/w6/w7 only — w3's change is evidenced by its checksummed same-SHA checkpoint artifact and w5 by decision records in the w4/w6 trios; the earlier w{0..6} glob claim was corrected rather than left dishonest")
             (holds-not-relitigated . "the W4 scheduler hold (queue p50 692.5 s / 761.5 s vs batch 637 s / 610 s at n=5), the W5 prepared-env warm-restore hold, and the W6 target-unachieved verdict (p50 935 s vs 588 s, p95 957.5 s vs 735 s) are restated with their observed numbers; no speedup claim is made for any held lever and the thresholds are not revised")
             (release-language . "the CHANGELOG entry names every topology change (lint split, fast-env overlap, telemetry relocation, protected-check graph), every hold, and the rollback rehearsal; README metrics synced to the tree (test lines 263061 after the BUG-0009 de-literalization) and the metrics lint passes 5/5; version surfaces agree at 1.00.26")
             (rollback-ordering-preserved . "every surface that mentions the rehearsal keeps the fail-safe order: remove the new protection requirement (lint-quality) first, restore workflow/policy state second, lint required throughout; the rehearsal's dry-run evidence is checksummed per wave plus the integrated binding")
             (gate-evidence-scope . "the .gate-evidence recordings bind the implementation HEAD and a fresh timestamp; they are untracked local artifacts by design and are re-recorded by the coordinator's lane at the merge state — the record does not claim they are durable wave artifacts")))
(concerns . ((coordinator-owned-release-steps . "the squash-merge, annotated tag at the merge SHA, protected-environment publish, and the post-release required-check re-audit are intentionally outside this record; the tag-publish readiness context expects a tag checkout or main, which cannot hold on the campaign branch by construction")
            (freshness-window . "the 7200 s gate-evidence freshness window means the recordings immediately preceding this return are the ones the coordinator's lane should consume; a lane run much later must re-record")))
(record-only . "this review adds no code and touches no digest input")
